1
00:00:02,519 --> 00:00:10,599
Chapter 2 Three nights later, Old Major died peacefully in his sleep.

2
00:00:10,599 --> 00:00:13,599
His body was buried at the foot of the orchard.

3
00:00:13,599 --> 00:00:15,839
This was early in March.

4
00:00:15,839 --> 00:00:20,480
During the next three months, there was much secret activity.

5
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:24,680
Major's speech had given to the more intelligent animals on the farm a

6
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:28,119
completely new outlook on life.

7
00:00:28,119 --> 00:00:33,559
They did not know when the rebellion predicted by Major would take place.

8
00:00:33,559 --> 00:00:37,799
They had no reason for thinking that it would be within their own lifetime,

9
00:00:37,799 --> 00:00:42,839
but they saw clearly that it was their duty to prepare for it.

10
00:00:42,839 --> 00:00:48,440
The work of teaching and organizing the others fell naturally upon the pigs, who

11
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:52,920
were generally recognized as being the cleverest of the animals.

12
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:59,519
Pre-eminent among the pigs were two young boars named Snowball and Napoleon,

13
00:00:59,519 --> 00:01:02,759
whom Mr. Jones was breeding up for sale.

14
00:01:02,759 --> 00:01:07,480
Napoleon was a large, rather fierce-looking Berkshire boar, the only

15
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:14,039
Berkshire on the farm, not much of a talker, but with a reputation for getting his own way.

16
00:01:14,039 --> 00:01:20,960
Snowball was a more vivacious pig than Napoleon, quicker in speech and more inventive,

17
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:25,160
but was not considered to have the same depth of character.

18
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:29,160
All the other male pigs on the farm were porkers.

19
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:35,079
The best known among them was a small, fat pig named Squealer, with very round

20
00:01:35,079 --> 00:01:41,039
cheeks, twinkling eyes, nimble movements, and a shrill voice.

21
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:45,119
He was a brilliant talker, and when he was arguing some difficult

22
00:01:45,119 --> 00:01:50,720
point, he had a way of skipping from side to side and whisking his tail,

23
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:53,640
which was somehow very persuasive.

24
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:58,000
The others said of Squealer that he could turn black into white.
